139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The Linear SVM achieved the highest fraudulent-class F1-score \(0.852\), with precision 0.862 and recall 0.842. Logistic Regression \(SGD\) achieved higher recall \(0.889\) but lower precision \(0.631\), meaning it identified more fraudulent postings while also flagging more legitimate postings. Decision Tree achieved recall 0.825 but low precision \(0.273\), resulting in a lower F1-score. Multinomial Naive Bayes achieved precision 1.000 but recall only 0.164, so it missed most fraudulent examples at the default threshold. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Accuracy measures the fraction of all correct predictions. Precision for fraud measures how many postings predicted as fraudulent were actually fraudulent. Recall for fraud measures how many actual fraudulent postings were detected. F1-score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall. ROC-AUC measures ranking discrimination across thresholds, while average precision summarizes the precision-recall curve and is particularly informative for imbalanced classification. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
